WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:11.100
47. The World's Oldest Sports. Soccer, baseball, volleyball, and golf. Humans

2
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:19.180
love sports. We play old ones. We invent new ones. We cheer for our favorite players and

3
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:24.460
cry over our losses. But how long have humans been playing sports

4
00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:32.500
for fun? Which sports are the oldest? Cricket, the English sport, is among the oldest.

5
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:38.340
There have been international cricket matches since 1844, but the game is much older than

6
00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:44.620
that. There are references to a sport called cricket as far back as the late 1500s when

7
00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:51.100
it was a children's game. It became popular among adults in the 1600s. The rules were

8
00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:59.680
officially recorded in 1744. Tennis is also quite old. It began in Europe. Experts believe

9
00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:05.960
it was played in monasteries for entertainment in the 1300s. It was first played with a wooden

10
00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:13.540
ball and with hands instead of rackets, but it evolved over time. It became popular among

11
00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:21.160
French kings between the 1500s and the 1800s. That was when it got the name tennis and when

12
00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:26.920
official rules were established. But by far, the oldest sport comes from the

13
00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:34.320
new world. It's called Yulama and it comes from what is now Mexico. Yulama was played

14
00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:41.400
on a long narrow court with two teams of four or five people at each end. Teams serve the

15
00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:46.040
balls to each other and then team members try to move the balls along the court until

16
00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:51.920
they score by hitting a ball past the other team's line. They can only hit the balls

17
00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:58.400
with their hips and thighs. Yulama is not common now, but it is still sometimes played

18
00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:05.760
today in parts of Mexico. It began as far back as 1500 B.C., which means Yulama has

19
00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:08.880
been played for 3,500 years.
